Patch 2913: MAX_DRAWS 4096 -> 8192 (experiment).

A 2 vs 2 on Hidden Leaf with the town in view has about 4,200-4,800 draws a frame. Above 4096 every frame was cut in two
batches (vp_flush_if_full, [MIDFLUSH] records=4088) and the second render_frame waited for the GPU to finish the first:
FTL draw about 33 ms instead of 16. With 8192 such a frame is one batch.

Tested (Experiments workbench, all-CPU 2 vs 2 on Hidden Leaf at 4K, SHADOW_SCALE=4, MODEL_DETAIL=4): [MIDFLUSH] 40+ lines
-> 1-2 per run, FTL draw about 33 -> 23 ms. The frame rate only followed with the frame clock's LATE_FLIP (port main.cpp).
The per-draw constant buffers grow with MAX_DRAWS.

